{{header transformations}}
'''Transformations''' alter Isaac's appearance and grant him special abilities.

A transformation occurs when obtaining at least three different [[item]]s from a particular set of items.<br>
These collectibles always share a particular theme that corresponds with the transformation.

== Transformation Sets ==
{{transformation table}}

== Requirements ==
* Items only need to have been acquired once in order to count.
** {{dlc|nr}} Duplicate items (like those acquired from {{i|Diplopia}}) do not count toward transformations when picked up. Only the first instance of an item Isaac owns will count.
** {{dlc|r}} Duplicate items are all counted.
** {{dlc|r+}} Duplicate items are not counted for the Necromancer transformation.
** [[Activated collectible]]s (e.g. {{i|Guppy's Head}}) can be picked up once and then swapped away with another without any loss to transformation progress.
* {{dlc|nr}} Rerolling items with a {{r|Dice Room}}, the {{i|D4}}, or the {{i|D100}} will not remove progress towards the transformation.
** {{dlc|r}} The transformation will be lost if the items required are rerolled or otherwise lost, eg. {{I|Sacrificial Altar|dlc=x}}.
* {{dlc+|a}} Familiars gained from {{i|Cambion Conception}} or {{i|Immaculate Conception}} do not count towards transformation progress.{{dlc-}}
* [[Trinket]]s do not count toward progress for any transformation, with the exceptions of {{t|Kid's Drawing}} that counts for Guppy transformation, {{t|Bob's Bladder|r+}} for Bob, and {{t|A Missing Page|r+}} for Necromancer.
* [[Pill]]s only count toward [[Adult]] and [[Stompy]], they do not count toward progress for any other transformation.
* Characters that start with an item that counts towards a transformation do count as one of the three items needed for a transformation, such as Judas starting with [[The Book of Belial]].
* {{dlc+|r}} Only the first character to pick up an item will gain progress towards its transformation. This applies in [[Repentance Co-Op|co-op]], or when playing as {{c|Jacob and Esau}} or {{c|Tainted Lazarus}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{C|Tainted Isaac}} will not lose a transformation nor progress towards it if he replaces an item that counts towards that transformation.

== Notes ==
* Transformations can be combined, keeping the effects of all transformations with no effects overriding others.
* Transforming into [[Beelzebub]] for the first time will unlock the ''Lord of the Flies'' [[achievement]] and {{i|Angry Fly}}.
* {{dlc|a}} As none of the Afterbirth transformations unlock an achievement or item, obtaining them is not required for 100% completion of the game in terms of achievements. However, this is only true if you unlocked {{i|Mom's Contacts}} on Rebirth, as the [[Yes Mother?]] transformation will happen once you collect three Mom items on Afterbirth and Afterbirth †.
* {{dlc|nr}} Many of the Afterbirth transformations override the charge animations of items such as {{i|Monstro's Lung}} and {{i|Brimstone}}, potentially making them more difficult to use.
** {{dlc|a+}} There is now an option to show a charge bar that floats above Isaac.

